          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::7a7aad00488e11d4a7c07f3f",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ],
          "value": "How can natural polysaccharides be rationally designed and utilized to overcome primary and acquired resistance to ICIs in solid tumors, given their complex structures and variable clinical outcomes?",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::00a97cdd8f787cbe68b388cb",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ],
          "value": "Natural polysaccharides (from fungi, plants, marine organisms) as immune adjuvants to overcome resistance to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs) in solid tumors. Covers structural biology, molecular mechanisms, preclinical/clinical evidence, translational challenges, and future technological directions.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::0b0c136f05c57c534c85bdf1",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ],
          "value": "This review systematically analyzes the potential of natural polysaccharides to enhance the efficacy of ICIs by reversing tumor immune resistance. It dissects the structure-activity relationships (SAR) governing immunomodulation, elaborates on four core mechanisms (TAM repolarization, CD8+ T cell rejuvenation, gut microbiota remodeling, and suppression of tumor-intrinsic escape), and evaluates current clinical translation bottlenecks such as structural heterogeneity and low bioavailability. The paper positions polysaccharides within the broader landscape of combination therapies, compares them with other adjuvants, and proposes a roadmap for precision medicine using AI-driven glycomics, synthetic biology, and multi-layer biomarkers.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::ee7e3572d67dbf2f67526363",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Introduction sections detailing primary/acquired resistance rates, limitations of CAR-T and kinase inhibitors, and the need for novel adjuvants."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::17a10ba46be35c4952913371",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Section 5.1 comparing polysaccharides with dual checkpoint blockade, TIM-3 targeting, and oncolytic viruses in terms of efficacy and safety profiles."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::fb8e4e0564c5b23f7abc6821",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "broader_review_uses"
          ],
          "value": {
            "material": "Sections 6.3-6.6 discussing AI-driven QSAR, graph neural networks, synthetic biology, and large-scale N-glycomics."
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::757541f80ab481e594311373",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "Most evidence is preclinical (mouse models) or from small early-phase human trials; causal links in humans are inferred from FMT experiments and observational cohorts.",
            "contribution": "Details the role of gut microbiota in mediating ICI response, specifically highlighting how polysaccharides remodel microbial composition (enriching Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolite profiles (increasing SCFAs like butyrate and propionate) to enhance anti-tumor immunity.",
            "facet_id": "F1"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::000bb7f76afc0e764242ec8f",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "Mechanisms are often derived from in vitro or syngeneic mouse models; direct translation to human clinical outcomes is not fully validated.",
            "contribution": "Elaborates on the molecular mechanisms of polysaccharide-mediated immunomodulation, including TAM repolarization (M2 to M1), CD8+ T cell exhaustion reversal, and suppression of tumor-intrinsic escape (PD-L1 downregulation). Links these to specific structural motifs (triple helix, acetylation).",
            "facet_id": "F2"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::d2525176a96ae5b3ac60e2bc",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions"
          ],
          "value": {
            "boundaries": "Based on specific dysbiotic mouse models; human relevance requires further validation.",
            "contribution": "Discusses the safety boundaries and risks associated with polysaccharide/fiber supplementation, noting that excessive fermentation in dysbiotic guts may lead to adverse outcomes like cholestatic liver cancer.",
            "facet_id": "F1"
          },
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::3eefb31b9abaa8d1b9d67ad1",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "The review focuses on natural polysaccharides; do not generalize findings to all prebiotics or dietary fibers without specifying the polysaccharide type.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::f2c5255f64a830040e1f35d7",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "Clinical evidence is primarily from early-phase trials or real-world retrospective studies; avoid overstating efficacy as if confirmed by Phase III RCTs.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
          "raw_source_handle": "P0152"
        },
        {
          "atom_id": "atom::8e35d942ffc4974b5cd35989",
          "source_handle": "P0152",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "scope_interpretation_cautions"
          ],
          "value": "Mechanistic claims are largely supported by preclinical models; distinguish between observed associations in mice and validated causal mechanisms in humans.",
          "role": "evidence",
          "snapshot_ids": [
            "snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b"
          ],
          "author_chapter_id": "Ch5",
          "author_messages_path": "F:\\OptoMind-Review-2\\outputs\\guided_body_compact_auto_metadata_20261009_12cny\\LIVE\\stages\\author_005\\c8a8e196a35945b70bab58ac7d25825d55761abfe16e04e3930ca8753de1bb61\\attempt_001\\MESSAGES.json",
